# Normalize line endings to LF in the repo.
#
# Rationale: on 2026-10-04 a branch flip from LF to CRLF silently inflated the
# diff on ~14 files (up to 1536 added/removed lines each) and forced a manual
# cleanup. Enforcing LF at the repo level means Windows checkouts that would
# otherwise rewrite files to CRLF no longer produce that churn, and `git diff`
# reflects real content changes only.
#
# PowerShell scripts target Windows and are kept as CRLF (the least-surprising
# default for the platform they run on).
* text=auto eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
# Binary assets: never treat as text (no newline rewriting, no "LF will be
# replaced" noise).
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
